{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/858425-using-ascension-in-horror","id":858425,"title":"Using Ascension in horror","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-03T11:47:53-07:00","id":858425,"title":"Using Ascension in horror","content":"One of the things I've liked the most about Scion is the gradual slide from human to God. Reflecting on how different my characters are now compared to their low legend days, I started to wonder if that loss of humanity could be used to give Scion a horror flavour. Has anyone here ever used a 'loss of humanity' theme in their games? What ways are there to make an Scions' gradual Ascension something horrific?<br /> NB: When I say ascension, I'm referring to the Scions journey from Legend 2 all the way to Lengend 12, not just the transition from 8 to 9.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T17:59:26-07:00","id":858639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/858425-using-ascension-in-horror#post858425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things I've liked the most about Scion is the gradual slide from human to God. Reflecting on how different my characters are now compared to their low legend days, I started to wonder if that loss of humanity could be used to give Scion a horror flavour. Has anyone here ever used a 'loss of humanity' theme in their games? What ways are there to make an Scions' gradual Ascension something horrific?<br /> NB: When I say ascension, I'm referring to the Scions journey from Legend 2 all the way to Lengend 12, not just the transition from 8 to 9.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I suppose it would depend on which mythos they're associating themselves with. I would imagine that joining the Aztecs would be quite horrifying, given how they conduct themselves. Nobody likes being told they will spend the rest of eternity ritually dismembering people for a good cause. They'll like it even less when they're selected to be the sacrificial victim in some kind of super ritual!<br /> <br /> <br /> Then there's the Norse. Congratulations, you're a God. Enjoy it while you can, because you're going to die horribly!<br /> <br /> <br /> Then we have the Greeks... Just... just the Greeks! Anybody who's read their mythology has to be VERY careful about what they say and do around them.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want to make ascension to Godhood something to be feared, remember that these pantheons are from the days of paganism and contain excessive amounts of violence, rape and cruelty. Anybody who pauses to think about that instead of focusing on the perks would understand that these are not very nice groups of people to hang around with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T21:18:06-07:00","id":858755,"title":"","content":"I've also seen it happen with people pushing Epic Intelligence. The horror isn't so much in what pantheon they're from and what those pantheons do as their gradual disassociation . They seem to become focused on achieving their goals and less impressed with how their actions and plans affect others. I've watched it happen as a fellow player, and as a ST, and the gradual decline makes it the scariest part, as they justify things and then that sets precedents that further down the track allow them to justify other things. And you watch it happen gradually, as someone who wants to use their intellect to make things better slowly, over time, follows a chain of events of logic that lead them toward some truly horrible behaviours. And in many times they couldn't even explain it even if they wanted to, because nobody would understand them.<br /> <br /> \u200bI saw it happen with a player who was running Doctor Aaron Tigrillo. After a while Aaron simply refused to talk to mortals at all, as he said that it was like talking to a puppy. They may be eager to listen and learn but they can't understand anything coming out of your mouth. Then, after a while, he drifted away from the band when they couldn't hold a conversation with him either. He would just take action, often horrible action, and when called on it would answer (if he answered at all) with &quot;You wouldn't understand. Give it a few years. Then you'll see what I've done.&quot;. <br /> <br /> By the end of it Aaron was barely recogniseable as human. He had no empathy for anything human or mortal, not because he was a bad person but because only creatures of a deific nature were able to understand anything he was saying, so he felt, as he said, 'no more pity for exterminating them than they do exterminating millions of microscopic organisms in a glass of water that they want to drink.'. <br /> <br /> In the end the player ended up giving up the character because it was freaking him out and he wanted to play something more upbeat and 'heroic'. Can't say I blamed him. But the curious part is that, by associating with him, the rest of the band were kind of drawn into the whole idea that the attrocities he committed were OK simply by not intervening or trying to stop him because 'he may be a freak but he's one of us'. Looking back I can see the effects the character had on the other characters, who were drawn down a darker road than they may have been.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T22:10:05-07:00","id":858776,"title":"","content":"This is a very interesting question! It is very close to my favorite theme of Scion, one of culture clash. The past is a different country, and all that.<br /> <br /> What I find is that most characters start to... slip up, sometimes as early as late Hero. It's slow, and normally very culture specific, but I have seen... I think maybe five Scions ever reach mid-Demigod and hold onto their 'humanity' to any real substantial degree. Only one to ever make it to God with it intact. None of these were mine, I tend to totally wander off the deep end sooner or later and start snatching up ancient values, finding compromises in areas most pivotal to the character's mortal life. Piety tends to sink the 'humanity' ship rather quickly as it encourages Scions to follow in the footsteps of the ancient culture which spawned their Pantheon.<br /> <br /> What I will say is that Nyrufa is exceptionally correct that it will very a huge degree Pantheon to Pantheon. For example, I would struggle to show this 'Loss of Humanity' theme playing a Tuatha Scion, the Irish Pantheon is already so human it is hard to tell where Divine ends and Mortal begins. If someone <i>really</i> wanted to, however, I would suggest they play a child of Fand, Niamh, Goitne, or one of the other Fairy-Entities who are related to Manannan. However, the Greeks, and Mesopotamians are the ripest for this 'loss of humanity' as their Gods are exceptionally different from humanity. The Greeks see mortals as little more than gadflies when they are not lusting after them, and are at their core almost all horrible people, even within their own culture. The Mesopotamian Pantheon legitimately created humanity to serve as a slave race after the Lesser Gods, who were previously enslaved, got uppity. To them, mortals are nothing.<br /> <br /> I would actually disagree with Nyrufa about the Aztecs however. The human sacrifice looks <i>very</i> grizzly to us, but makes total sense from their perspective. And, if all myths are true, they are <i>right</i> about this. The Teotl (Aztec Pantheon) actually are one of the few Pantheons who <i>care</i> about humanity. Maybe not on an individual level, but damn it, they've lost <i>five</i> worlds so far and they're really trying with this one. The blood sacrifices, preformed by both mortals and by the Teotl themselves, are to fuel the Pantheon to preserve the world. Huitzilopotchli must carry the sun and defend it, Xipe Toltec needs to keep the corn growing, ect. Normally Aztec Scions are super freaked out about it all, since, you know, it's hard to get behind, even with their Virtues screaming at them to toe the line. But what I think is that after they experience the Aztec afterlives, it's totally reasonable. If you get sacrificed, you get to go to one of the several not-Mictlan underworlds. You're killing, but it guarentees them a spot in one of the good afterlives (Mictlan is one of the most horrific underworlds, up there with Irkalla and Yomi) and helps ensure the world doesn't end. Which it has, four times so far. It's not an unreasonable worry. However! The Teotl are not a fun place for modern Scions for other reasons. Homosexuality is a death sentence. Women are not in a good position IIRC. <br /> <br /> So after writing all of this, I would actually like to slightly readjust my initial idea that Scion could entirely run with the theme of a 'loss of humanity' as a Scion grows in power. I think it <i>can</i> but is very Pantheon dependent. To some Pantheons it would be difficult (Bogovi, Tuatha, Orisha) to lose touch with mortals without also losing touch with the Pantheon. However, what I think all Scions can experience is a dramatic shift in values, or having to fight against values being forced upon them. While they may not struggle to lose their humanity, they will almost certainly struggle to maintain their modern perceptions of the world. While a Tuatha Scion will likely be human even after reaching Legend 12, they will be obsessed with how they are perceived, their social standing, constantly wanting to show others up and bask in the glory. It is human... but, well, two millennium late, give or take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T23:21:36-07:00","id":858791,"title":"","content":"Ah, I was not aware the sacrifice thing was a guaranteed cushy spot in the next world. But the reason I suggested the Aztecs is because the culture they founded no longer exists, or at least not on the grand scale it used to. Scion takes place in the modern age, and you don't just go around in public carving out people's hearts and drinking their blood to keep the universe in motion. Also keep in mind that the Aztecs seem to gain the most amount of power by sacrificing their own relatives instead of random strangers.<br /> <br /> Imagine if you receive a visitation, being told you're a hero, then being handed an obsidian knife and told to go on a killing spree because daddy needs his pint of blood for the day. That would be some traumatic shit for somebody born and raised in the modern world.<br /> <br /> <br /> Canonically (in the pre-made story), Aaron is not happy about his status as a God. The constant blood sacrifices have shaken his faith and he questions whether they truly need as much blood as they claim to. Which goes to show that not every Aztec is happy with what they have to do, even if it does serve the greater good.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then there's Blair Thomas who happens to be homosexual. Rather than put him to death, his father skins a woman and creates a flesh suit that will allow his son to change sex. You tell me how somebody in touch with their humanity is supposed to react to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-04-2016, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T09:15:58-07:00","id":859055,"title":"","content":"By freaking out? Then slowly being drawn into it. Like Watcher said, the Virtues can really drive this, though, in our experience, Conviction was the road straight to hell with Piety several steps behind. Others can lead there pretty quickly as well. In a game run by Telgar, at VERY low Legend, the Tuatha (me) and the Aesir went off the deep end very early on via Courage and drove the group crazy trying to stop us from going on a cop-killing spree. (Admittedly, crooked thrall cops)<br /> <br /> We really started seeing this whole &quot;slide&quot;, in our latest Scion game (and, probably, last - sorry but I can't abide the rules breakdown at Demigod and lots of what's going into Scion 2.0 leaves me cold, particularly some of the more outre collectible card like aspects of the rules). It wasn't really a morally-centered group to begin with, but some of the characters just stopped caring immediately:<br /> <br /> The daughter of Erzulie Freda changed to the morality of a cat from the get go. She just didn't care how her wishes (whims, really) affected people. Like deciding mid-flight that she wanted the commercial air plane to go somewhere else. Which ended up with a lot of distressed passengers (once they left her Epic Charisma-y) present. The pilots lost their jobs (and, in fact were arrested, she changed it into an international flight). She wasn't even THAT concerned about the fuel. (She knew she could probably walk away from a crash or hitch a ride after a safe landing). <br /> <br /> The son of Tangaroa (from the Maori pantheon) wasn't a nice guy in the slightest to begin with, but he definitely stopped caring about anything mortal that didn't affecting him directly or even the more humane cares of most of the divinities he dealt with. Sure, he was a trickster-type from a criminal background, but he just became an outright bastard, to the point that he was just using the other characters to further his own ends but was so useful, the characters were typically okay with it. <br /> <br /> But our son of Huitzopochtli was actually a pretty good guy. At the start of the game, his job was trying to recover kidnapping victims. He definitely didn't like &quot;bad guys&quot;. But hunting bad guys and dealing with them made perfect sense to him. And it was actually not easy for him NOT to kill them. So, ya know, if they are dead already (and there are some father issues where impressing daddy lurks in the background), why not cut off their heads and start building a tzompantli? And from there, things started getting much darker fairly quickly. A rude racist bartender reluctantly serving Erzulie's daughter a drink? Cut off his hand. Mortals do not disrespect his companions. It wasn't too long before he and the son of Tangaroa grabbed a homeless guy and sacrificed him in a bath tub as a <i>stunt </i>for a Prophecy roll. (Oh there was still a last rationalization, they picked a guy who was suicidal already. Of course, he was suicidal because they largely talked him into it using Epic Manipulation...)<br /> <br /> Even the one mostly unalloyed good guy in the group, a son of Ganesha who spent part of his vast fortune to set up elephant reserves and on charities to feed the poor, etc. (elephants first, starving children second) ended up shacking up with a human-eating rakshasa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T15:09:59-07:00","id":859279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/858425-using-ascension-in-horror?p=859055#post859055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By freaking out?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly. But I'm not suggesting that it's scary for the character. I'm saying from a player stand point. Unless the OP is asking how to make it seem scary for the characters as well as the players. in which case, I think the suggestions I originally posted are good ways to go. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T06:23:50-07:00","id":859584,"title":"","content":"Basically when you become a god at essence 9 you are no longer human, your body is pure ichor and you can remake yourself as you see fit.<br /> <br /> Scion players are domed to be less and less human even at character creation those who take epic appearance are maybe the first to see what change happen with their surrounding. Player with horrific appearance learn pretty fast that if they go openly normal people will run away in fear and that cast them aside from humanity whereas those with beautifu appearance get all the attention and are soon easily corrupted in abusing people adoration.<br /> <br /> The question that comes to my mind after writing this is &quot;when a human stop being human ?&quot;. I think my answer would be when a human get any signficant super power, that power make them different. Suddenly they are able to do impossible thing by human standart and either they hide from humanity inf fear of some backlash (in fear of humanity that kill what they can't control or understand) or either they go openly and are revered or feared by the mass their power define another standart in which their normal/previous life is no longer needed or welcomed.<br /> <br /> Power change people and change the view that other have on them I think and for the horrific part it's doable in showing how character player have changed from the point of view of one of their familly member or friend who are normal human being. Show them regularly the consequence of their action in the darkest light possible and you will slowly build the horrific sense that you are looking for I believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2799-astoril","name":"Astoril","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T10:17:33-07:00","id":859725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astoril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/858425-using-ascension-in-horror?p=859584#post859584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The question that comes to my mind after writing this is &quot;when a human stop being human ?&quot;. I think my answer would be when a human get any signficant super power, that power make them different. Suddenly they are able to do impossible thing by human standart and either they hide from humanity inf fear of some backlash (in fear of humanity that kill what they can't control or understand) or either they go openly and are revered or feared by the mass their power define another standart in which their normal/previous life is no longer needed or welcomed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It could also be whenever the human gains significant enlightenment. As somebody on the road to godhood, the Scions are exposed to powers and secrets that mortals were never meant to know, either because they can not be trusted, or because they are incapable of accepting it. Your character has privileges that mortals can only dream of, but they also have responsibilities, too. Like the saying goes &quot;you can't please everyone&quot; and the needs of the many outweigh the needs of the few. <br /> <br /> To a particular group of people, the Scion's actions may seem monstrous, but in the grand scheme of things, it may have been to serve a greater good. After all, they're not just battling supernatural terrorists, they're battling the very incarnations of nature itself. If they lose, it's the apocalypse, so there's not a lot of room for error when the whole world is at stake, and sometimes morality becomes more of an inconvenience, rather than a strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T16:55:22-07:00","id":859975,"title":"","content":"To get horror in Ascension, you don't need to be a God. You don't need to have Epic Intelligence. You don't even have to embrace the lifeways and beliefs of another radically different culture. <br /> <br /> You just have to roleplay your Virtues. Even the &quot;friendlier&quot; ones are hardcore. Courage 3, Epic Strength and Divine Wrath vs. a belligerent 8 year old can end in a bad place. The not-so-nice ones are dead awful if you want to keep something like a Western humanist moral center. <br /> <br /> Though it certainly doesn't hurt if you're the Scion of Mictlantecuhtli, your Calling is &quot;Saint of Cannibals&quot; and your Visitation story involves being locked in an van with a dozen men women and children crossing the Mexican/USA border that has been abandoned in the desert in the hot hot sun for several days.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T20:20:32-07:00","id":860074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/858425-using-ascension-in-horror?p=859975#post859975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You just have to roleplay your Virtues. Even the &quot;friendlier&quot; ones are hardcore. Courage 3, Epic Strength and Divine Wrath vs. a belligerent 8 year old can end in a bad place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Who wants daddy's belt?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T02:10:45-07:00","id":860185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/858425-using-ascension-in-horror?p=859975#post859975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You just have to roleplay your Virtues. Even the &quot;friendlier&quot; ones are hardcore. Courage 3, Epic Strength and Divine Wrath vs. a belligerent 8 year old can end in a bad place. The not-so-nice ones are dead awful if you want to keep something like a Western humanist moral center.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you go a bit extreme with your example, sure when you enter virtue extremity thing can go really bad but you don't have to roll courage when a harmless child insult you. IMO you roll your virtue when it is dramatically appropriate not everytime something happen.<br /> <br /> When you think about it, there are many hook to go horror in scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2799-astoril","name":"Astoril","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T08:15:50-07:00","id":860317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astoril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/858425-using-ascension-in-horror?p=860185#post860185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you go a bit extreme with your example, sure when you enter virtue extremity thing can go really bad but you don't have to roll courage when a harmless child insult you. IMO you roll your virtue when it is dramatically appropriate not everytime something happen.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe... But if it's not &quot;dramatically appropriate&quot; why are playing through it? Do you play through long drives in real time? Eating meals at a fast food place? Trouble going to sleep? Watching a favorite TV show or game? Probably not. Unless you're playing it for setting to start a scene where something else is going to happen very soon or just to give context to the fast-fading mundane aspects of human life. We don't see much of those sort of things (or analogues thereof) in myths either. In either case, it's a dramatic situation, so the Virtues become relevant. <br /> <br /> Notice I stated &quot;Courage 3&quot;. That is the start of &quot;The deeper the commitment... the harder it becomes for a Scion to resist acting according to his beliefs, even when such action might be dangerous or unwise&quot;(Hero p.117). That's when acting counter to the tenets of the Virtue or wising to refrain from acting in accord with the Virtue start invading pretty much everything the Scion does. An ex-significant other coming up and slapping a Scion would count as a running against up to potentially three of the tenets. It's not a Virtue Extremity (that requires a lot more build-up), it's just acting the way the ichor flows. Sure, a Courage 1 character might get a pass. Probably a Courage 3 character, but, if that slap is part of the action in the scene (and why are you having it occur &quot;on camera&quot; when it's not), then it's definitely something that has to be considered.<br /> <br /> Virtues are not largely toss away stats like Nature is (until WP is way down and the finagling starts), they are the veritable Sword of Damocles hanging over the Scions' heads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T09:57:58-07:00","id":860388,"title":"","content":"Not to mention that the Gods typically don't care who's offending them; all that matters is they did so.<br /> <br /> Hell, just look at what Hera did because of Zeus. Made life a living hell for Scions who couldn't possibly be held responsible for their father's actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T08:06:02-07:00","id":861051,"title":"","content":"In my game I don't play only important or dramatic action. Sometimes my players want to interact in some non meaningfull way with their surrounding, talking human in stupid scheme just for fun or things like that. So maybe we don't play the same way and don't have the same view on virtue because of that.<br /> <br /> But anyway I don't see any interest in virtue that force players to play like robot just because some trait named virtue tell them to play all the action of their character in a strict and rigid way. No fun in that. And as I reread it nothing in the book tell you that virtue impose themself on every action of your character if not every god of the same pantheon would be the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2799-astoril","name":"Astoril","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T10:10:46-07:00","id":861122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/858425-using-ascension-in-horror?p=860388#post860388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, just look at what Hera did because of Zeus. Made life a living hell for Scions who couldn't possibly be held responsible for their father's actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you may be looking at this from a very human point of view. Hera was goddess of wives and motherhood but as queen of the gods she was a goddess of justice as well. Zeus stood above her and she couldn't punish him or bring him to justice as he was exempt from all that as king. The crime of adultery had been committed against her and her Vengeance virtue just won\u2019t allow this to go unpunished. The only people she can punish are the women Zeus slept with and the evidence of the crime, his children. Worse, they keep ascending to godhood and taking up seats on the council as a form of constant mockery of Zeus\u2019 rampant infidelity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T10:30:38-07:00","id":861137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astoril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/858425-using-ascension-in-horror?p=861051#post861051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my game I don't play only important or dramatic action. Sometimes my players want to interact in some non meaningfull way with their surrounding, talking human in stupid scheme just for fun or things like that. So maybe we don't play the same way and don't have the same view on virtue because of that.<br /> <br /> But anyway I don't see any interest in virtue that force players to play like robot just because some trait named virtue tell them to play all the action of their character in a strict and rigid way. No fun in that. And as I reread it nothing in the book tell you that virtue impose themself on every action of your character if not every god of the same pantheon would be the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one said that. I certainly didn't. The real limitations on their actions are limited to the factors that run counter to the Virtue. And those apply ALL THE TIME. You don't get to be cowardly in your personal life and go all berserker when the giants show up. You have COURAGE. It defines the Scion. It flows through his/her veins and empowers her divine nature. And they do so relative to the number of dots in the Virtue, but, even then, it's a lot easier to go along with your Virtue even at 1 dot. So, yeah, every god in the pantheon is acting according to the same Virtues (except for the weirdos with substitutes). That's part of what defines the character of the pantheon. They are acting in accord with their different degree of investment in those Virtues. Witness Achilles' (the poster, not the demigod) discussion of Hera and her Vengeance of 5. Zeus probably doesn't have Vengeance 5, but I doubt he could be said to have less than 3 based on some of his over-reactions. And even the easiest-going of the Greek gods seems to get all vengeance-y over the most minor of transgressions (say, Hermes... He isn't quite as bad as many of the others, but he did have his moments, so, say, Vengeance 1). But they don't get to put their Virtues in a box just because it's supper-time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T16:39:24-07:00","id":861420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/858425-using-ascension-in-horror?p=861122#post861122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you may be looking at this from a very human point of view. Hera was goddess of wives and motherhood but as queen of the gods she was a goddess of justice as well. Zeus stood above her and she couldn't punish him or bring him to justice as he was exempt from all that as king. The crime of adultery had been committed against her and her Vengeance virtue just won\u2019t allow this to go unpunished. The only people she can punish are the women Zeus slept with and the evidence of the crime, his children. Worse, they keep ascending to godhood and taking up seats on the council as a form of constant mockery of Zeus\u2019 rampant infidelity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Right, that's the point I was trying to make.<br /> <br /> <br /> How do you portray ascension as something horrifying?<br /> <br /> Simple, just think about how the old Gods conduct themselves, and about all the innocent people that got hurt because of their petty squabbles.<br /> <br /> How long will it be before your character steps on a rival's toes and they go after somebody who did nothing wrong just so they could spite you?<br /> <br /> Worse yet, how long will it be until you decide to do the same thing because your rival is too powerful to tackle head on?<br /> <br /> <br /> Looking at Ascension from a God's point of view, it's not really terrifying. It's just routine business; you have to look at it from a human point of view to get the horror across of what you are about to become and what you could potentially do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T21:07:37-07:00","id":861573,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that your character can find it horrifying. Not after they first get visited at Legend 2 and they get their virtues. There would be a period where you would realize that you have never behaved this way before or you never felt this strongly/passionately about certain things but lets face it once you get used to your virtues and that adjustment period I doubt you constantly lament your characters actions, feelings and reactions to everything. There is a war going on, there are people that need saving, you have missions that would instantly be made into movies if you told the tale, half the time you should have barely time to think because the titanspawn are needing to be dealt with.<br /> <br /> I suppose in some quiet moments of reflection you may mourn the person you used to be as some kind of sacrifice or casualty of war but that implies the person you are is monstrous or someone the old you wouldn't like.. That sort of thing may crop up from time to time in Hero level of play as you still most likely have dealings with the people in the circles you traveled in before getting visited but most games I've been in have followed the idea that 1) most scion gaming time you spend adventuring/investigating things that get more and more fantastical/mythological as your legend goes up so human reminders happen pretty much in your downtime 2) you get your Virtues at the very start of the game and that is the biggest psychological change to the character you created for pre-visitation. Most people I have gamed with don't raise their Virtues with xp after that so its rare that you get 'nuttier' or more extreme so you figure out the 'new you' and move on, otherwise you and your bandmates are pretty much having the same arguments at demigod and god levels that you had when you first got together and had to learn to cope with not only your own virtues but most likely some rather opposing ones depending on which pantheons everyone came from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}